x716 write x715 2
x717 text "A file starts with zero or more `use \"path.a0\"` lines, relative to the file. The linker loads every used file once, orders them by dependency, and validates the result as one program with one namespace. Cycles are rejected. A function name defined in two files is rejected with both locations. Diagnostics on a linked program name the file and line they belong to."
x718 puts x716 x717
x719 call close x718 
x720 call open x719 10
x721 write x720 4
x722 write x721 2
x723 text "code"
x724 puts x722 x723
x725 call open x724 4
x726 write x725 2
x727 text "use \"ui.a0\"\nuse \"../examples/life.a0\"\nfn page io -> io\na call open p0 5\nb call close a\nret b\nend"
x728 puts x726 x727
x729 call close x728 
x730 call close x729 
x731 call close x730 
x732 call open x731 13
x733 write x732 4
x734 write x733 1
x735 text "editing"
x736 puts x734 x735
x737 call open x736 11
x738 write x737 2
x739 text "Views and edits"
x740 puts x738 x739
x741 call close x740 
x742 call open x741 2
x743 write x742 2
x744 text "A model never sees a whole file. It asks for a view of one function: the function with a handle line on top (e0) and, when the whole program matters, a program handle (g0) with one signature line per function. A reply is the handle line followed by edits, one per line: `id op ...` replaces the instruction id or inserts it before ret; `id op ... @ other` inserts after other; `-id` deletes; `ret x` changes the result. Under g0, a whole `fn ... end` block adds or replaces a function and `-fn name` removes one. The edit is applied only if it parses, type-checks, validates, and was written against the current revision; otherwise it is rejected and the handle stays valid."
x745 puts x743 x744
x746 call close x745 
x747 call open x746 10
x748 write x747 4
x749 write x748 2
x750 text "code"
